superman-recomp L9-A oracle trace, v2 (iter-463 burndown) - against xenia-canary-oracle
(canary_experimental @ 0bd090dbe979bc64959efe519aa320db8e3eb467).

Supersedes xenia_trace.patch + xenia_trace_jitprolog.patch for the ORACLE tree (those two
remain for reference/xenia-canary @ 0b4e6c4). Adds, on top of the v1 hooks:
  - XENIA_GUEST_TRACE_VAS: JIT-time function-entry filter (only listed functions get the
    prolog call; everything else is stock code), so a whole boot-to-gameplay run is cheap;
  - XENIA_GUEST_TRACE_ICALL_FUNCS / XENIA_GUEST_TRACE_ICALL_BAD: an X64Emitter::CallIndirect
    call-site hook that records indirect-call targets (tag 2 = from a listed function,
    tag 3 = target outside [0x820F0000,0x8290F5B8) or misaligned, i.e. exactly our
    PPC_CALL_INDIRECT_FUNC "out-of-range" condition).
Record format unchanged (XENTRC01 + 32-byte records). Unit test: test_xenia_trace.cpp.

TO APPLY (from reference/xenia-canary-oracle):
    cp ../../tools/xenia-trace/xenia_trace.h src/xenia/cpu/xenia_trace.h
    git apply ../../tools/xenia-trace/xenia_trace_oracle.patch
BUILD (separate output dir; never touches the user's Xenia install):
    see tools/xenia-trace/README.md "Oracle v2 build".
